# ---- build output ----
/Zenith.exe
/Zenith.exe~
*.exe
!core/mihomo.exe
*.test
*.out

# ---- runtime state (regenerated on first run) ----
/data/state.json
/data/state.json.*
/data/config.yaml
/data/proxy-snapshot.json
/data/candidates.txt
/data/cache.db
/data/nodes.json
/data/ui-profile/
/data/ASN.mmdb
/data/*.part
/logs/

# ---- intentionally tracked, do NOT ignore ----
#   core/mihomo.exe     the proxy core
#   data/zenith.ico     the application icon
#   data/GeoSite.dat    rule database, so a fresh clone starts in a second
#   data/geoip.metadb   rule database, same reason

# ---- editors / OS ----
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- go ----
/vendor/
# ---- runtime state that must never be committed ----
#
# config.last-good.yaml is the rollback copy of the generated configuration. It
# is a full configuration: the same node credentials the subscription carries.
# It was committed by accident when the configuration transaction was added, and
# a credential in a public history is a credential that has to be replaced.
/data/config.last-good.yaml
/data/config-transaction.json
/data/tun-transaction.json
/data/candidates.stat.json
/data/activation.yield

# The control secret grants control of the core's configuration API, which is
# enough to redirect every connection this machine makes. It was tracked for seven
# commits before this line existed - the file-level ACL did not help, because git
# does not read ACLs. Rotate it if it has ever been pushed: deleting a file from a
# repository does not remove it from the history other people already have.
/data/control.secret